<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikandar Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1358–1390</span> · Also known as Sikandar Shah of Bengal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikandar-lodi">Sikandar</a> Shah was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> from 1358 to about 1390, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamsuddin-ilyas-shah">Shamsuddin Ilyas Shah</a>. He withstood a second invasion by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firuz-shah-tughluq">Firuz Shah Tughluq</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1359, which ended in a negotiated peace confirming Bengal's independence. He built the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adina-mosque">Adina Mosque</a> at Pandua, completed in the 1370s. He was killed in battle against his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyasuddin-azam-shah">Ghiyasuddin Azam Shah</a>.</p></div>
